edit(4,[('The conductor may be stationary as a body; carrier drift already constitutes current and permits magnetic force.','Bulk translation is not required for the current-force law.'),('Magnetic force requires bulk translation; carrier drift in a stationary wire can produce only a voltage.','The current-carrying stationary wire can experience force, not only motional voltage.'),('Bulk translation is required only when the wire current is perpendicular to the field.','Perpendicular current maximizes this force but does not impose body translation.'),('A nonzero wire force requires both external current and a separately induced motional EMF.','An externally supplied current in a stationary wire is sufficient when the current has a transverse field component.')])
