edit(6,[('v×B is zero for parallel motion.','The stated vector model therefore gives zero motional EMF along any rod direction.'),('Only the speed magnitude matters, so the EMF equals Bℓv even when velocity is parallel to B.','The scalar perpendicular special case cannot replace the cross product for parallel velocity.'),('An open rod must carry a pre-existing DC current before any motional EMF can exist.','An open conductor may develop charge separation without a sustained pre-existing current.'),('The rod-axis projection alone gives Bℓv; the angle between velocity and field can be ignored.','The integrand first contains v×B, which vanishes before any projection when v is parallel to B.')])
