edit(43,[('Current sets torque in the constant-flux model, while speed also follows voltage, back EMF and load balance.','Electrical and mechanical operating conditions must be compatible.'),('Current alone fixes speed because every load has the same torque-speed relation.','Different mechanical loads can have different torque-speed characteristics.'),('At fixed current, changing supply voltage cannot change back EMF or speed.','V=RI+V_b allows the back EMF to change when V changes at fixed I.'),('Voltage and current fix the electrical operating point, so mechanical load balance can be omitted from a steady-speed test.','A claimed steady operating point must also balance motor and load torques.')]);cite(q(43),1693,'equation','T=K_t I and V_b=K_vω under constant flux.');cite(q(43),1694,'equation','Steady current balance and torque-speed equation.');cite(q(43),1710,'figure','Motor/load torque intersection at the common operating speed.')
